# Everything in this repository is read by Linux: Docker builds, entrypoint
# scripts, dbt, CI. A CRLF file breaks some of them outright — a shell script
# with CRLF fails inside a container with `bad interpreter: no such file`, which
# names the interpreter and not the real cause.
#
# It happens without anyone deciding to do it: on Windows, Python's `open(...,
# "w")` translates "\n" to "\r\n", so an ordinary edit script rewrites an entire
# file's line endings. The diff then shows every line as changed and the real
# change is invisible. That is exactly how it happened here.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.pptx  binary
*.onnx  binary
*.joblib binary
*.parquet binary
*.duckdb binary
*.avro  binary
